<id/19/1934/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Benjamin"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_gums_resins_naval_stores/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "an odoriferous gum-resin, obtained in Siam, and the Eastern Archipelago, from *Styrax Benzoin*, and used in perfume and license. It is of a yellowish gold colour with occasionally white almond-like masses in it; there are, however, two or three varieties which enter into commerce. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 46]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_gums_resins_naval_stores): Named gum-resin under an archaic spelling (olibanum; 'Benjamin' = benzoin, Simmonds 1892 s.v. BENJAMIN; 'camphire' = camphor) left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 2 rows, 1800–1800. Series: KEW_CUST 5 ×2. Units: Lasts ×2. Top routes: World → United Kingdom ×1; East Indies and China → United Kingdom ×1."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <id/scheme/#resource> ;
    skos:notation "1934" ;
    skos:prefLabel "Benjamin"@en ;
